seg-81df4f5cd02e = Inside the container the server must listen on <c1/>, so it needs <c2/> and the token. Publishing the port as <c3/> keeps it on your machine; drop the <c4/> only when you mean to expose it, and then terminate TLS in front of it. <c5/> and Fly.io and Cloud Run templates are in <a1><c6/></a1>.

