seg-c33701cb9ca2 = <a1><c1/></a1>: take the token from Secret Manager

# text
# c1: --allowed-host
seg-b86ddb72b916 = Each runs the published image, sets <c1/> to the platform hostname you replace in the file, and relies on the platform for HTTPS.

# text
seg-ce3a5326cb95 = Set a CPU and memory limit on the platform

# text
# c1: cpus
# c2: mem_limit
# c3: [[vm]]
# c4: resources.limits
# c5: --max-concurrent
seg-e1fc13672597 = The timeout, pool and budget bound how much work is admitted, but one admitted call can still use a core for a long time and a large result can use hundreds of megabytes. Put a hard limit on the container as well: the templates ask for { "2" } CPUs and { "1" } GiB (<c1/> and <c2/> in Compose, <c3/> in Fly, <c4/> in Cloud Run). Keep <c5/> at or below the CPU count.

# text
seg-058781b052c4 = What it is not

# text
seg-90edc7ff2a55 = Not a multi-tenant service. Anyone holding the token runs simulations on your hardware; there are no per-user quotas beyond the limits above.

# text
seg-5b3b9c610f31 = Advisory, not type-approved navigation equipment: the operator remains responsible for navigation. The simulator's outputs are modelled or validated figures for analysis, as everywhere else in Kshana.

